Title: Last Ticket
Credit: original short drama; names, events and dialogue are new
Author: Claude (draft)
Format: 6 scenes x 16 s (each scene = 2 Flow generations of 8 s, one shot each), English dialogue
Tests: a two-person drama built from the playbook alone; a placed prop (jar, coins, ticket) and no hand-to-hand passing; a second location after a context card

INT. HOLLOWAY STATION TICKET OFFICE - NIGHT

[[look: small railway ticket office at night, wooden counter with a brass-framed ticket window on the right, roll-down shutter above the window, round wall clock, green-shaded desk lamp, glass entrance door on the left with rain on it, worn brown suitcase on the floor behind the counter]]

MARA VOSS, sixties, the station's ticket clerk, pulls the roll-down shutter of her window halfway down. The wall clock reads 10:31. Behind her, a worn suitcase waits by the back door.

THEO KEANE, early twenties, bursts through the glass door out of the rain and crosses to the window, a glass jar of coins in both hands.

THEO
One ticket to Halden. Please.

INT. HOLLOWAY STATION TICKET OFFICE - NIGHT

MARA looks at the clock, then at him over her glasses, and does not lift the shutter.

MARA
We closed at half past ten.

THEO glances at the platform door behind him, then back at her.

THEO
The machine only takes cards.

INT. HOLLOWAY STATION TICKET OFFICE - NIGHT

THEO sets the jar of coins on the counter beneath the shutter.

THEO
Mine's declined. This is all I have.

MARA looks at the jar, then up at the wall clock. It reads 10:44.

MARA
Last train's ten-fifty.

INT. HOLLOWAY STATION TICKET OFFICE - NIGHT

MARA takes off her glasses. Her eyes go to the suitcase behind her, then to THEO, who waits without a word.

MARA pushes the shutter all the way up.

MARA
Pour it out. We'll count it.

THEO tips the jar and the coins spill across the counter.

INT. HOLLOWAY STATION TICKET OFFICE - NIGHT

MARA counts the coins into small stacks with quick, practised fingers.

MARA
Fourteen eighty. Exactly the fare.

MARA brings the date stamp down on a ticket with a heavy thump and lays it on the counter. THEO picks it up.

THEO
Thank you.

EXT. HOLLOWAY STATION PLATFORM - NIGHT

[[marker: context card "10:50 p.m."; second location, open platform in light rain]]

The headlights of the last train sweep the wet platform. THEO waits with the ticket in his hand. MARA walks out of the office behind him, the suitcase at her side, and he turns.

THEO
You're coming too?

THEO and MARA stand side by side as the train doors slide open and the light falls across them.

MARA
Last train. Last shift.
